jumpgate test workloads
========================

Independent "protected server" sshd workloads for the jumpgate kind demo/e2e.
These are NOT part of the jumpgate control-plane deployment; each stands in for
a real target host that an admin onboards via the CLI, exercising a different
asset credential type:

  - sshd.{Dockerfile,yaml} + entrypoint.sh
        CA-trusting target (TrustedUserCAKeys). Service/Deployment: ssh-target.
        Login: deploy. Auth: warden-CA-signed user certificate.

  - sshd-password.{Dockerfile,yaml} + entrypoint-password.sh
        Password target. Service/Deployment: ssh-target-password.
        Login: demo. Password: demo-password-123.

  - sshd-key.{Dockerfile,yaml} + entrypoint-key.sh
        Public-key target. Service/Deployment: ssh-target-key.
        Login: demo. Authorized key: demo_key.pub.

THROWAWAY TEST KEYS
-------------------
demo_key / demo_key.pub is an ed25519 keypair generated with:

    ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' -C jumpgate-test-key -f demo_key

It is committed ON PURPOSE for the automated tests ONLY. It is a throwaway,
non-secret, test-only credential: the private key is the stored asset key for
ssh-target-key in the e2e, and the public key is baked into that target's
authorized_keys. DO NOT reuse it anywhere real.
